  "id": "ependymoma",
  "term": "ependymoma",
  "definition": "Ependymoma is a glioma that develops from ependymal cells lining the brain’s ventricular system or the central canal of the spinal cord. It can occur inside the skull or in the spine, tending to be more often malignant in children when intracranial and more often benign in adults when intraspinal.",
